apt-blitz (0.9.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reject 200-OK responses to Range requests on multi-segment downloads
    instead of silently truncating head-of-file bytes at segment offsets.
  * Pin upstream ETag via If-Match on every segment; abort download when
    the upstream file changes mid-download (412) to avoid mixed-generation data.
  * Verify xz stream integrity (xz --test) before storing .xz files in cache.
  * Log etag and last-modified metadata on cache store.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Fri, 15 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.8.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Log remaining time-to-expiry (ttl_secs) when a request is served from a
    fresh cache hit.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.8.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Forward upstream HTTP status code to the client instead of 502 when
    upstream HEAD returns an error (404, 403, etc.).
  * Forward Location header so clients can follow upstream redirects.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cache freshness: revalidate cached files against upstream via
    conditional HEAD (If-None-Match / If-Modified-Since).
  * New --max-cache-age option (default 86400s) to serve fresh-by-age
    entries without contacting upstream.
  * Migrate cache DB schema: add cached_at column with backfill.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.7.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Configurable coalesce follower timeout and max retries.
  * Replace retry loop with single long-wait for in-flight downloads.
  * Fix all clippy warnings.
  * Fix OOB tests and consistent 400/502 error responses.

